w: 1.~Sound the bat- tle cry!|See, the foe is nigh;|Raise the stand- ard high|for the_ Lord;|
w: 2.~Strong to meet the foe,|march- ing on we go,|While our cause we know|must pre- * vail;|
w: 3.~O Thou God of all,|hear us when we call,|Help us one and all|by Thy_ grace;|
 F4 F4 D3 E F4 | G4 e4 d3 c B4 | d4 f4 B3 A B2 c2 | d4 c4 B8 || %8
w: Gird your ar- mor on,|stand firm eve- ry one;|Rest your cause up- on His|ho- ly Word.|
w: Shield and ban- ner bright,|gleam- ing in the light,|Bat- tling for the right we|ne’er can fail.|
w: When the bat- tle’s done,|and the vic- t’ry’s won,|May we wear the crown be-|fore Thy face.|
